x86_64-linux  cxx1 emits the complete-object C1 constructor of Box where clang, on this target, emits only the base-object C2 of an inline constructor and calls it - the same difference base-implicit-constructor-emitted.nonames records. arm64-darwin and x86_64-windows agree on every name, the friend's own included; the extra C1 is a mergeable superset. What this case is about, a friend defined in the class body reaching a private member, is checked by run.sh on all three machines.
